# Android (TWA)
# The generated Gradle project is build output — `node scripts/build-twa.mjs`
# recreates it. twa-manifest.json is generated too, from the environment.
android-twa/
# Signing keys never go in a repository. Play ties an app to its key forever:
# a leaked key lets someone else ship an update to your users, and a lost one
# means republishing under a new listing.
*.keystore
*.jks


# The signing key password lives beside the key; neither belongs in git.
*.keystore.pass
*.pass.*.bak

# Scratch copies of host config, pasted in for debugging
temp/
my-publishing-studies/competition.md

# Answers and thinking, not part of the repository.
/notes/

# Everything about the box this runs on: its firewall, its mail ports, its
# backups, the other machines that watch it. A private repo of its own, because
# how one particular server is built is not a fact the public repo should carry.
# See server/README.md.
server/

# ── Kept on disk, kept out of the repo ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# These are how this is being built rather than what is being built: the queue,
# the planning, the working notes, the agent instructions. All of it is still
# here and still used — it is just nobody else's business, and a public repo
# ships its whole history.
#
# CONTRIBUTING.md carries the parts of AGENTS.md that a contributor needs.
